THE PLATFORM PORT: no environment, no layers, and one way to load a driver.

WHAT THIS PATCH IS FOR, AND WHY IT IS SEPARATE FROM 0001. The portable-static-target patch declares
the platform surface and defines nothing; it is what makes the candidate surface measurable. This one
describes BEHAVIOUR - what this platform answers when the loader asks it something - and it belongs
to the derived half of the lockfile, after pass 1 has measured and before pass 2 links.

IT IS APPLIED TO A COPY, NEVER TO THE PINNED TREE. The static-target pin froze three archives built
WITHOUT it, and both builds have to stay reproducible, so the ported sources live beside the pinned
ones and the builder is told which of the two to compile.

WHAT IT CHANGES, IN TWO FILES:

  loader_environment.c  TWO CHANGES. LiberSystem takes upstream's own third shape - the one its `#else` branch
                          already provides for a platform with no environment variables - rather than
                          the common-unix one it joined for its file and thread facilities. Reading
                          an environment is the ambient search this configuration exists to refuse:
                          an overridable layer path, an overridable driver selection and an
                          overridable log level are three ways for something outside the verified
                          closure to decide what runs inside it. `loader_secure_getenv` is defined
                          here too, which upstream's branch does not do, because its callers are
                          compiled on this platform and are not on the ones that branch was for.
                          And the id-filter override PARSER loses its body, which is not the same
                          change twice: with the reader answering NULL the optimiser already deleted
                          everything below its first branch, so the artifact was correct either way -
                          but the SOURCE still called `strtoul`, and a sysroot that must declare a
                          function the substrate does not provide is the general POSIX layer arriving
                          through the include path. An empty filter is what an unset variable
                          produced anyway, so no behaviour changes.
  loader.c              the two layer-scan entry points answer an EMPTY list. That is legal under
                          the specification and true here: there is no layer directory, no layer
                          manifest and no way to load one. Everything downstream then follows from
                          upstream's own code - `vkEnumerateInstanceLayerProperties` reports zero, and
                          an instance or device creation that ENABLES a layer is refused with
                          `VK_ERROR_LAYER_NOT_PRESENT` by the lookup that does not find it. These two
                          functions are the ONLY entry points into the layer manifest search, so
                          replacing them removes the filesystem walk, the settings-file override and
                          the environment-steered layer paths in one place rather than in fifty.
                        AND `VK_LUNARG_direct_driver_loading` IS REMOVED. The extension hands the
                          loader a driver's own lookup in an instance's create info, and upstream then
                          negotiates with that driver directly - at the version it asks for, with no
                          substrate between them - and takes the physical-device function out of the
                          same lookup: both the bounded negotiation and the two-export rule, passed by
                          anything that holds a driver's lookup, and its exclusive mode skips the scan
                          the record answers. A list in the create info now calls nothing,
                          `loader_add_direct_driver` goes with it, and the extension is not advertised,
                          so an instance that enables it is refused with
                          `VK_ERROR_EXTENSION_NOT_PRESENT` by upstream's own validation - which runs
                          after the driver scan and before any driver is created.

WHAT IT MEASURABLY REMOVES FROM THE SURFACE: `getenv`, the four identity queries `is_high_integrity`
needed, and `strtoul`, which was reached only to parse a number an environment variable carried. Six
symbols, 58 to 52, on all three targets - and six declarations out of the profile sysroot with them,
because what the substrate does not provide is not declared. The direct-driver path takes nothing
out of it: that path called only the loader's own functions and the pointers it was handed.

WHAT IT DOES NOT REMOVE, AND WHY IT CANNOT: the provider-open and manifest-read facilities the layer
path SHARED with the ICD path stay, because they are the same symbols and the ICD path is what this
substrate exists to serve. What they reach on this system is a bounded, package-owned record rather
than an ambient directory - the discovery item's decision, not an accident of this port.

